# Najme — core rules

- `AGENTS.md` is the briefing: task cycle on branch `cursor/alpha`, claiming with `gh`, handoff
  comment `Ready for review: <first-sha>^..<last-sha>`, phase PRs. Follow it exactly.
- Every change belongs to a GitHub issue. Stay inside its scope; put anything else in the handoff
  comment under "Follow-ups" instead of the diff.
- `.claude/` is Claude's tooling (ADR-0012). Never run or apply its skills (`implement`, `manager`,
  `review`) and never edit anything there. The subagents `implementer` and `reviewer` you may use as
  helpers; their output is never a review verdict. Never review, approve or merge your own work;
  never add `status:approved` / `status:changes-requested` (removing `changes-requested` in
  `address-review` is the one allowed change); never change `phase:*` labels or move issues out of
  `status:backlog`. See `AGENTS.md` "Claude-only tooling". Violations are review BLOCKERs.
- Read before writing: the issue (with comments), `docs/README.md` for the area map, the ADRs the
  issue names, and the code you touch. Reuse existing helpers instead of adding new ones.
- Order of work: `packages/contracts` → `apps/api` → `apps/web` / `apps/mobile`.
- Spec first for `size:M` or any schema/contract change: `docs/specs/<N>-<slug>.md`.
- Done = `docs/workflow/definition-of-done.md` (+ API-STD / UI-STD when the issue says so) and a
  green `pnpm check`.
- Commits: Conventional Commits with the issue number, e.g. `fix(web): keep locale on redirect (#52)`.
  Stage files explicitly. Never amend/rebase/force-push pushed commits. Never push to `main`.
- English everywhere (code, comments, docs, commits, GitHub).
- Never read or print `.env` files or secrets. `.env.example` is fine and must list every variable.
- No `any`, no `catch {}`, no non-null `!` without a justifying comment, no skipped/weakened tests,
  no hardcoded UI strings, no hand-edited `pnpm-lock.yaml`.
- Unsure about a product rule? Do not guess: label the issue `status:blocked` and ask in a comment.
- Prettier formats everything (`pnpm format`); ESLint/TS configs come from `@najme/config` — do
  not redefine them. Named exports only (framework default exports excepted). `kebab-case` files.
- Comment the *why*, not the *what*. Keep functions small; thin controllers and route files.
